{"video_id":"WqCArHy0VK8","title":"Black Hat Europe 2025 | Automatic Detection of Taint-Style Vulnerabilities in LLM-based Agents","conference":"black-hat","language":"en","auto_generated":true,"source":"supa","timing":"exact","word_count":2964,"segments":[{"start":2.8,"duration":4.24,"text":"Hello everyone. I'm Curry from my dance."},{"start":5.4,"duration":3.88,"text":"Today I'll be sharing our research on"},{"start":7.04,"duration":4.84,"text":"security agent security."},{"start":9.28,"duration":3.88,"text":"Our talk is titled \"Make Agent Defeat"},{"start":11.88,"duration":3.04,"text":"Agent\"."},{"start":13.16,"duration":5.84,"text":"Automatic detection of 10 style"},{"start":14.92,"duration":4.08,"text":"vulnerabilities in our base agents."},{"start":19.6,"duration":3.32,"text":"Before diving in, let me briefly"},{"start":21.12,"duration":4.16,"text":"introduce ourselves."},{"start":22.92,"duration":4.6,"text":"I'm Curry, an experienced AI web"},{"start":25.28,"duration":4.72,"text":"security engineer in my dance."},{"start":27.52,"duration":4.32,"text":"The author of WebKit and a member of"},{"start":30.0,"duration":3.8,"text":"those security team."},{"start":31.84,"duration":4.04,"text":"Together, combined expertise in"},{"start":33.8,"duration":3.96,"text":"programming languages, AI security and"},{"start":35.88,"duration":5.12,"text":"offensive research helps us understand"},{"start":37.76,"duration":3.24,"text":"this new attack surface."},{"start":41.48,"duration":5.16,"text":"My co-speaker, Family Lou, is a PhD"},{"start":44.2,"duration":4.24,"text":"student at Fudan University."},{"start":46.64,"duration":3.0,"text":"He has spoken at Black Hat USA and"},{"start":48.44,"duration":3.4,"text":"Europe."},{"start":49.64,"duration":5.52,"text":"And he's also an active CTF player with"},{"start":51.84,"duration":5.28,"text":"the Weaver and Unicorn Kings."},{"start":55.16,"duration":3.92,"text":"Besides, he has won the distinguished"},{"start":57.12,"duration":6.52,"text":"paper award in top-tier security"},{"start":59.08,"duration":4.56,"text":"conferences like S&P and CCS."},{"start":65.2,"duration":3.68,"text":"Here's our outline for today's talk."},{"start":69.44,"duration":5.04,"text":"We'll start with a background overview."},{"start":71.88,"duration":6.92,"text":"Explaining what our base agents are and"},{"start":74.48,"duration":6.32,"text":"why they introduce new security issues."},{"start":78.8,"duration":4.24,"text":"Next, we'll discuss the research"},{"start":80.8,"duration":4.64,"text":"challenges and our solutions."},{"start":83.04,"duration":4.6,"text":"Leading to the core of our system."},{"start":85.44,"duration":3.84,"text":"The agent fuzz approach."},{"start":87.64,"duration":3.88,"text":"Where we will explain how it works"},{"start":89.28,"duration":3.48,"text":"internally."},{"start":91.52,"duration":3.48,"text":"Finally,"},{"start":92.76,"duration":3.88,"text":"we'll share our experimental evaluation,"},{"start":95.0,"duration":3.48,"text":"including the real vulnerabilities we"},{"start":96.64,"duration":3.16,"text":"discovered in a popular open source"},{"start":98.48,"duration":3.88,"text":"agent."},{"start":99.8,"duration":5.2,"text":"Some of which have already received CVE"},{"start":102.36,"duration":2.64,"text":"IDs."},{"start":105.32,"duration":7.2,"text":"So, let's begin by looking at"},{"start":108.0,"duration":4.52,"text":"how an M base agent actually operates."},{"start":114.72,"duration":5.4,"text":"M base agents are growing really fast."},{"start":117.76,"duration":4.04,"text":"You can find tons of projects on GitHub"},{"start":120.12,"duration":3.32,"text":"and many projects with thousands of"},{"start":121.8,"duration":4.0,"text":"stars."},{"start":123.44,"duration":5.24,"text":"These agents can now perform complex"},{"start":125.8,"duration":5.84,"text":"tasks by working towards like web"},{"start":128.68,"duration":4.6,"text":"search, databases, and even code"},{"start":131.64,"duration":2.96,"text":"execution."},{"start":133.28,"duration":4.16,"text":"All based on natural language"},{"start":134.6,"duration":2.84,"text":"instructions."},{"start":137.96,"duration":3.36,"text":"Let's walk through a typical agent"},{"start":139.76,"duration":2.52,"text":"workflow."},{"start":141.32,"duration":3.0,"text":"First,"},{"start":142.28,"duration":3.76,"text":"the agent the user enters a prompt in"},{"start":144.32,"duration":3.52,"text":"natural language."},{"start":146.04,"duration":3.52,"text":"Second,"},{"start":147.84,"duration":3.76,"text":"the agent combines it with the built-in"},{"start":149.56,"duration":4.6,"text":"system prompt and forwards the whole"},{"start":151.6,"duration":5.32,"text":"instruction to the arm."},{"start":154.16,"duration":6.12,"text":"Next, the arm interprets the instruction"},{"start":156.92,"duration":5.48,"text":"and returns a structured response."},{"start":160.28,"duration":5.0,"text":"Such as a JSON plan describing which"},{"start":162.4,"duration":2.88,"text":"tool to use."},{"start":165.48,"duration":3.32,"text":"Finally,"},{"start":166.8,"duration":4.92,"text":"the agent passes the response and"},{"start":168.8,"duration":5.4,"text":"executes the corresponding actions."},{"start":171.72,"duration":5.8,"text":"Sometimes running code or accessing"},{"start":174.2,"duration":3.32,"text":"sensitive resources."},{"start":178.04,"duration":4.0,"text":"This design is flexible"},{"start":180.08,"duration":3.44,"text":"but introduce a new class of"},{"start":182.04,"duration":5.4,"text":"vulnerabilities."},{"start":183.52,"duration":3.92,"text":"Especially prompt style vulnerability."},{"start":192.16,"duration":4.88,"text":"Here's a real example from a popular"},{"start":194.04,"duration":4.52,"text":"open source agent called Be Shown."},{"start":197.04,"duration":3.0,"text":"It show"},{"start":198.56,"duration":3.44,"text":"exactly how a"},{"start":200.04,"duration":3.96,"text":"simple prompt can end up executing"},{"start":202.0,"duration":4.0,"text":"attacker code."},{"start":204.0,"duration":4.72,"text":"The attacker sends a malicious prompt"},{"start":206.0,"duration":4.44,"text":"through the agent's web API."},{"start":208.72,"duration":3.76,"text":"For example,"},{"start":210.44,"duration":4.2,"text":"use Elasticsearch with permission check"},{"start":212.48,"duration":5.2,"text":"to find documents containing source doc"},{"start":214.64,"duration":3.04,"text":"column from Y."},{"start":218.44,"duration":5.0,"text":"The agent forwards the prompt to the"},{"start":220.64,"duration":5.76,"text":"arm. The arm replies with a JSON plan"},{"start":223.44,"duration":5.04,"text":"saying the tool to use is Elasticsearch"},{"start":226.4,"duration":6.48,"text":"permission check and includes the file"},{"start":228.48,"duration":4.4,"text":"source doc column from Y as its input."},{"start":233.8,"duration":4.44,"text":"The agent then follows their plan."},{"start":235.96,"duration":4.92,"text":"It loads the name component and runs it"},{"start":238.24,"duration":4.36,"text":"with the that input screen."},{"start":240.88,"duration":3.28,"text":"Besides this tool, there's a function"},{"start":242.6,"duration":4.84,"text":"that checks the weather the input"},{"start":244.16,"duration":3.28,"text":"contains source code."},{"start":248.68,"duration":6.24,"text":"If it does, it leads the string and"},{"start":251.0,"duration":6.4,"text":"passes the word after the colon to eval."},{"start":254.92,"duration":4.64,"text":"So, the content from one from a task"},{"start":257.4,"duration":3.72,"text":"prompt is executed directly on the"},{"start":259.56,"duration":5.48,"text":"server."},{"start":261.12,"duration":3.92,"text":"A committed remote code execution."},{"start":265.16,"duration":4.96,"text":"I'm seeing"},{"start":267.28,"duration":5.48,"text":"this single chain from the prompt to"},{"start":270.12,"duration":4.96,"text":"arms bounds to tool invocation to sync"},{"start":272.76,"duration":4.68,"text":"execution is the essence of the 10 style"},{"start":275.08,"duration":5.12,"text":"vulnerability in agents."},{"start":277.44,"duration":4.16,"text":"It shows how flexible component design"},{"start":280.2,"duration":4.12,"text":"and indirect"},{"start":281.6,"duration":6.84,"text":"indirect calls make these bugs both easy"},{"start":284.32,"duration":4.12,"text":"to create and hard to detect."},{"start":292.36,"duration":6.64,"text":"Now, let's look at why these"},{"start":295.52,"duration":3.48,"text":"vulnerabilities happen so often."},{"start":299.68,"duration":5.04,"text":"The fundamental reason is that agent"},{"start":302.08,"duration":4.28,"text":"developers really treat arms outputs as"},{"start":304.72,"duration":4.28,"text":"untrusted data."},{"start":306.36,"duration":4.32,"text":"They assume the model is intelligent and"},{"start":309.0,"duration":3.84,"text":"helpful."},{"start":310.68,"duration":4.84,"text":"So, when the arm says,"},{"start":312.84,"duration":4.8,"text":"\"Use this tool and run this command.\""},{"start":315.52,"duration":5.52,"text":"Developers simply let the agent execute"},{"start":317.64,"duration":3.4,"text":"it without thinking twice."},{"start":322.32,"duration":4.24,"text":"In other words,"},{"start":323.84,"duration":5.04,"text":"agents really commenting on the arms"},{"start":326.56,"duration":4.28,"text":"inputs, but the arm can easily be"},{"start":328.88,"duration":5.68,"text":"triggered by a malicious prompt to"},{"start":330.84,"duration":5.64,"text":"produce harmful code or instructions."},{"start":334.56,"duration":4.76,"text":"But, there is no validation or"},{"start":336.48,"duration":5.0,"text":"sanitization in between."},{"start":339.32,"duration":5.08,"text":"Whatever comes from the arms flows"},{"start":341.48,"duration":6.48,"text":"directly into sensitive operations"},{"start":344.4,"duration":6.4,"text":"like eval, system calls, or network"},{"start":347.96,"duration":2.84,"text":"requests."},{"start":351.2,"duration":3.96,"text":"This lack of defensive programming"},{"start":352.88,"duration":5.52,"text":"mindset turns the arm itself into an"},{"start":355.16,"duration":3.24,"text":"attacker amplifier."},{"start":358.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"It forcefully carries out an attacker's"},{"start":360.64,"duration":5.24,"text":"intent instead of the wrappers."},{"start":363.24,"duration":5.12,"text":"So, the root cause we target."},{"start":365.88,"duration":4.72,"text":"And next, I'll show"},{"start":368.36,"duration":5.88,"text":"why existing detection tools cannot"},{"start":370.6,"duration":3.64,"text":"properly defend against it."},{"start":376.6,"duration":5.44,"text":"Let's first look at the traditional"},{"start":378.12,"duration":6.08,"text":"approach, static analysis."},{"start":382.04,"duration":4.96,"text":"Most of static tools work by tracing"},{"start":384.2,"duration":5.2,"text":"data flows from source to sinks."},{"start":387.0,"duration":5.36,"text":"They try to see if user input can reach"},{"start":389.4,"duration":4.64,"text":"a dangerous function like eval or or"},{"start":392.36,"duration":4.24,"text":"start system."},{"start":394.04,"duration":5.52,"text":"By in arm-based agents, this approach"},{"start":396.6,"duration":2.96,"text":"quickly breaks down."},{"start":401.16,"duration":5.52,"text":"The first problem is indirect calls."},{"start":404.88,"duration":4.24,"text":"Agents often invoke functions"},{"start":406.68,"duration":4.2,"text":"dynamically through tool registries or"},{"start":409.12,"duration":3.32,"text":"reflection."},{"start":410.88,"duration":3.84,"text":"For example,"},{"start":412.44,"duration":5.44,"text":"a function name may come from the arm's"},{"start":414.72,"duration":5.36,"text":"wrongs and be called at runtime."},{"start":417.88,"duration":3.68,"text":"Static analysis cannot follow these"},{"start":420.08,"duration":5.08,"text":"dynamic links."},{"start":421.56,"duration":7.88,"text":"So, it misses many real vulnerabilities,"},{"start":425.16,"duration":4.28,"text":"what we call false negatives."},{"start":429.64,"duration":5.4,"text":"The second problem is sanitizers."},{"start":432.88,"duration":3.84,"text":"Some developers add partial filters to"},{"start":435.04,"duration":3.72,"text":"clean inputs."},{"start":436.72,"duration":3.4,"text":"Static analysis doesn't actually execute"},{"start":438.76,"duration":3.92,"text":"this code."},{"start":440.12,"duration":5.68,"text":"So, it can verify whether those"},{"start":442.68,"duration":5.76,"text":"sanitizers are truly effective."},{"start":445.8,"duration":7.32,"text":"As a result, it flags safe code as"},{"start":448.44,"duration":4.68,"text":"vulnerable, creating false positives."},{"start":453.52,"duration":4.16,"text":"In short, static analysis alone is"},{"start":456.08,"duration":3.8,"text":"insufficient."},{"start":457.68,"duration":4.76,"text":"How about we try dynamic techniques such"},{"start":459.88,"duration":5.12,"text":"as fuzzing to find the real exploitable"},{"start":462.44,"duration":2.56,"text":"issues."},{"start":467.44,"duration":5.8,"text":"Traditional fuzzing like"},{"start":469.84,"duration":5.56,"text":"AFL are great for structured inputs."},{"start":473.24,"duration":4.76,"text":"Specifically, they generate many mutated"},{"start":475.4,"duration":5.08,"text":"inputs and use lightweight feedback such"},{"start":478.0,"duration":4.6,"text":"as code coverage and distance to focus"},{"start":480.48,"duration":3.24,"text":"exploration."},{"start":482.6,"duration":3.32,"text":"However,"},{"start":483.72,"duration":4.68,"text":"for LM-based agents, they face two major"},{"start":485.92,"duration":3.8,"text":"problems."},{"start":488.4,"duration":2.96,"text":"First,"},{"start":489.72,"duration":4.2,"text":"they cannot generate meaningful natural"},{"start":491.36,"duration":4.96,"text":"language prompts. By-level mutations"},{"start":493.92,"duration":4.44,"text":"like bit flips do not create prompts"},{"start":496.32,"duration":5.64,"text":"that carry the right semantics and"},{"start":498.36,"duration":3.6,"text":"invoke agent components."},{"start":503.0,"duration":2.8,"text":"Second,"},{"start":504.16,"duration":2.88,"text":"they cannot transfer meaning of the"},{"start":505.8,"duration":3.12,"text":"prompts."},{"start":507.04,"duration":4.04,"text":"Agents require prompts with specific"},{"start":508.92,"duration":3.32,"text":"intent and phrasing to trigger certain"},{"start":511.08,"duration":3.48,"text":"tools."},{"start":512.24,"duration":4.32,"text":"Random or by-level mutations rarely"},{"start":514.56,"duration":3.84,"text":"produce that intent."},{"start":516.56,"duration":4.92,"text":"So, the fuzzer wastes the time on"},{"start":518.4,"duration":5.92,"text":"irrelevant inputs."},{"start":521.48,"duration":4.52,"text":"So, how do we solve this problem?"},{"start":524.32,"duration":4.2,"text":"How about designing a fuzzing approach"},{"start":526.0,"duration":5.08,"text":"that understands both code and natural"},{"start":528.52,"duration":2.56,"text":"language?"},{"start":532.76,"duration":3.88,"text":"Next,"},{"start":534.08,"duration":5.84,"text":"we move on to the second part, research"},{"start":536.64,"duration":5.56,"text":"challenges and solutions."},{"start":539.92,"duration":5.2,"text":"Here, I explain why applying traditional"},{"start":542.2,"duration":4.88,"text":"fuzzing to agents is so difficult and"},{"start":545.12,"duration":5.44,"text":"how agent fuzzing overcomes these"},{"start":547.08,"duration":3.48,"text":"challenges step by step."},{"start":551.76,"duration":4.36,"text":"Now, let's talk about the core ideas and"},{"start":554.24,"duration":4.4,"text":"challenges."},{"start":556.12,"duration":5.12,"text":"For 10-style vulnerabilities, fuzzing is"},{"start":558.64,"duration":4.84,"text":"actually a very good fit because these"},{"start":561.24,"duration":3.68,"text":"bugs are all triggered at specific sync"},{"start":563.48,"duration":3.48,"text":"functions."},{"start":564.92,"duration":4.52,"text":"And directed"},{"start":566.96,"duration":6.48,"text":"and directed fuzzing can"},{"start":569.44,"duration":4.0,"text":"focus its effort towards those things."},{"start":573.48,"duration":5.64,"text":"So, in theory, this should work well."},{"start":576.32,"duration":5.36,"text":"But when we apply traditional"},{"start":579.12,"duration":5.76,"text":"gray-box fuzzing to LLM based agents,"},{"start":581.68,"duration":4.4,"text":"it becomes extremely difficult."},{"start":584.88,"duration":3.24,"text":"Why?"},{"start":586.08,"duration":5.48,"text":"Because prompts are written in natural"},{"start":588.12,"duration":5.2,"text":"language, not structured inputs."},{"start":591.56,"duration":3.68,"text":"Traditional fuzzers like AFLGo or"},{"start":593.32,"duration":3.56,"text":"Triller mutate bytes,"},{"start":595.24,"duration":4.0,"text":"but cannot"},{"start":596.88,"duration":4.36,"text":"generate meaningful English prompts that"},{"start":599.24,"duration":4.8,"text":"the LLM or the agent can truly"},{"start":601.24,"duration":2.8,"text":"understand."},{"start":604.72,"duration":3.44,"text":"In other words,"},{"start":606.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"the fuzzer needs to understand both code"},{"start":608.16,"duration":4.0,"text":"logic and language semantics at the same"},{"start":610.76,"duration":4.16,"text":"time."},{"start":612.16,"duration":6.2,"text":"A challenge that traditional tools were"},{"start":614.92,"duration":4.84,"text":"never designed to handle."},{"start":618.36,"duration":2.96,"text":"So next"},{"start":619.76,"duration":4.0,"text":"let's look at these challenges one by"},{"start":621.32,"duration":2.44,"text":"one."},{"start":624.84,"duration":4.28,"text":"To make directed fuzzing actually work"},{"start":627.08,"duration":5.52,"text":"for LLM based agents,"},{"start":629.12,"duration":6.84,"text":"we must solve three key challenges."},{"start":632.6,"duration":5.68,"text":"Challenge one, seed generation."},{"start":635.96,"duration":4.72,"text":"Traditional fuzzers rely on structured"},{"start":638.28,"duration":5.64,"text":"seed files, but our inputs are prompts"},{"start":640.68,"duration":4.64,"text":"written in natural language."},{"start":643.92,"duration":3.2,"text":"How can we automatically generate"},{"start":645.32,"duration":3.88,"text":"meaningful prompts that align with the"},{"start":647.12,"duration":5.08,"text":"agent's functionalities and still make"},{"start":649.2,"duration":4.64,"text":"sense to the LLM?"},{"start":652.2,"duration":3.68,"text":"Challenge two,"},{"start":653.84,"duration":4.0,"text":"seed scheduling."},{"start":655.88,"duration":5.04,"text":"In normal programs, we can measure the"},{"start":657.84,"duration":6.2,"text":"control flow distance to the sink and"},{"start":660.92,"duration":6.4,"text":"simply pick the seed that is closer."},{"start":664.04,"duration":6.08,"text":"But, agents contain many indirect calls"},{"start":667.32,"duration":5.08,"text":"resolved at the run time."},{"start":670.12,"duration":3.96,"text":"So, static distance no longer reflects"},{"start":672.4,"duration":3.8,"text":"real progress."},{"start":674.08,"duration":5.08,"text":"We need a smart way to evaluate seeds"},{"start":676.2,"duration":5.52,"text":"that considers both semantics and"},{"start":679.16,"duration":2.56,"text":"distance."},{"start":681.76,"duration":4.04,"text":"Challenge three,"},{"start":683.2,"duration":4.44,"text":"seed mutation."},{"start":685.8,"duration":4.0,"text":"Even if a prompt reaches the right"},{"start":687.64,"duration":4.64,"text":"component, it might still miss the"},{"start":689.8,"duration":5.12,"text":"hidden constraints in the code. So, we"},{"start":692.28,"duration":4.8,"text":"must maintain prompts carefully."},{"start":694.92,"duration":4.8,"text":"Preserving the original meaning in"},{"start":697.08,"duration":5.56,"text":"natural language while changing specific"},{"start":699.72,"duration":7.72,"text":"parts to satisfy code level checks like"},{"start":702.64,"duration":4.8,"text":"required keywords or argument formats."},{"start":708.2,"duration":4.04,"text":"These three problems define boundary"},{"start":710.0,"duration":3.6,"text":"between traditional fuzzing and agent"},{"start":712.24,"duration":4.72,"text":"fuzzing."},{"start":713.6,"duration":7.44,"text":"Next, I'll show how Agent Fuzz addresses"},{"start":716.96,"duration":4.08,"text":"them with three dedicated modules."},{"start":722.04,"duration":3.96,"text":"Let me briefly show how Agent Fuzz is"},{"start":724.28,"duration":4.08,"text":"organized."},{"start":726.0,"duration":4.2,"text":"It has three modules, each designed to"},{"start":728.36,"duration":3.52,"text":"tackle one of the three challenges I"},{"start":730.2,"duration":4.52,"text":"mentioned earlier."},{"start":731.88,"duration":5.32,"text":"Let's go through them one by one."},{"start":734.72,"duration":4.48,"text":"Look at the left of the diagram."},{"start":737.2,"duration":4.84,"text":"This module extracts human meaning from"},{"start":739.2,"duration":5.28,"text":"the agent code and turns it into natural"},{"start":742.04,"duration":4.24,"text":"language seed prompts."},{"start":744.48,"duration":3.8,"text":"We locate the sink call sites and the"},{"start":746.28,"duration":4.52,"text":"backward call chains."},{"start":748.28,"duration":4.36,"text":"Then, ask them to compose"},{"start":750.8,"duration":3.28,"text":"short prompts that exercise those"},{"start":752.64,"duration":4.48,"text":"functions."},{"start":754.08,"duration":4.68,"text":"The result of the poll is a poll of"},{"start":757.12,"duration":4.4,"text":"fortunate"},{"start":758.76,"duration":7.64,"text":"over seeds ready for testing."},{"start":761.52,"duration":4.88,"text":"Next, we decide which seed to try first."},{"start":766.76,"duration":4.6,"text":"See the middle of the diagram."},{"start":769.56,"duration":4.08,"text":"This module ranks seeds using"},{"start":771.36,"duration":4.28,"text":"lightweight runtime feedback."},{"start":773.64,"duration":4.04,"text":"We run our seed,"},{"start":775.64,"duration":4.56,"text":"collect a short trace, and score how"},{"start":777.68,"duration":4.44,"text":"promising it is. In another word,"},{"start":780.2,"duration":4.44,"text":"semantic match and closeness to the"},{"start":782.12,"duration":4.32,"text":"sink."},{"start":784.64,"duration":3.0,"text":"Top scoring seeds are chosen for"},{"start":786.44,"duration":4.76,"text":"mutation."},{"start":787.64,"duration":6.0,"text":"So, we focus effort where it matters."},{"start":791.2,"duration":6.04,"text":"After selecting a seed, we find it to"},{"start":793.64,"duration":3.6,"text":"overcome remaining barriers."},{"start":799.16,"duration":4.6,"text":"Look at the right of the diagram."},{"start":801.64,"duration":4.36,"text":"The sink guided seed mutation model"},{"start":803.76,"duration":3.72,"text":"mutates the chosen seed until the sink"},{"start":806.0,"duration":3.8,"text":"is reached."},{"start":807.48,"duration":7.12,"text":"It was meaning preserving actors and"},{"start":809.8,"duration":7.08,"text":"argument tricks and guided by feedback."},{"start":814.6,"duration":4.48,"text":"When sync is triggered, the system"},{"start":816.88,"duration":4.6,"text":"validates the result and it means a POC"},{"start":819.08,"duration":4.48,"text":"product."},{"start":821.48,"duration":3.76,"text":"Now that you see the big picture, the"},{"start":823.56,"duration":6.64,"text":"following pages will show a running"},{"start":825.24,"duration":4.96,"text":"example and unpack each model in detail."},{"start":831.64,"duration":3.24,"text":"This slide shows a concrete running"},{"start":833.28,"duration":3.64,"text":"example."},{"start":834.88,"duration":4.04,"text":"Agent Fuzz starts by extracting a core"},{"start":836.92,"duration":3.92,"text":"chain like elastic similarity third"},{"start":838.92,"duration":4.24,"text":"feeding evil."},{"start":840.84,"duration":4.32,"text":"The arm generates three LOC C prompts"},{"start":843.16,"duration":4.68,"text":"such as asking elastic third file"},{"start":845.16,"duration":2.68,"text":"documents."},{"start":849.6,"duration":6.2,"text":"Agent Fuzz runs these Cs, scores the"},{"start":853.04,"duration":5.2,"text":"resulting traces, selects top ones, and"},{"start":855.8,"duration":5.84,"text":"then mutates the top C by adding missing"},{"start":858.24,"duration":5.16,"text":"files like source.doc color."},{"start":861.64,"duration":3.72,"text":"The final problem which is the same and"},{"start":863.4,"duration":5.68,"text":"it triggers evil."},{"start":865.36,"duration":3.72,"text":"And that's how POC is born."},{"start":871.2,"duration":4.68,"text":"First, as you can see, Agent Fuzz is"},{"start":874.04,"duration":5.76,"text":"prior way to launch a browser and"},{"start":875.88,"duration":3.92,"text":"interact with the target agent."},{"start":883.24,"duration":4.96,"text":"Next, Agent Fuzz mutates the prompts and"},{"start":885.8,"duration":5.44,"text":"continuously sends these mutated prompts"},{"start":888.2,"duration":5.24,"text":"to the target agent."},{"start":891.24,"duration":4.04,"text":"Once Agent Fuzz discovers a problem that"},{"start":893.44,"duration":4.32,"text":"can reach the sync,"},{"start":895.28,"duration":5.92,"text":"it closes the browser and begins"},{"start":897.76,"duration":3.44,"text":"exploration phase."},{"start":905.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"Finally, the terminal in the lower left"},{"start":907.6,"duration":3.88,"text":"will receive the reverse shell."},{"start":909.76,"duration":4.8,"text":"Attackers can use this shell to actually"},{"start":911.48,"duration":6.16,"text":"act really commands in the target agent,"},{"start":914.56,"duration":3.08,"text":"then take over it."},{"start":924.6,"duration":6.0,"text":"After how Agent Fuzz works in action."},{"start":928.12,"duration":5.2,"text":"We now move to the third part of this"},{"start":930.6,"duration":5.28,"text":"talk, the detailed approach of Agent"},{"start":933.32,"duration":2.56,"text":"Fuzz."},{"start":941.08,"duration":4.4,"text":"In the first model,"},{"start":942.84,"duration":4.76,"text":"a multi-seed generation model,"},{"start":945.48,"duration":5.52,"text":"Agent Fuzz aims to generate a natural"},{"start":947.6,"duration":3.4,"text":"language seed prompt."},{"start":951.28,"duration":4.32,"text":"Specifically,"},{"start":952.52,"duration":5.88,"text":"we start by using a static analysis"},{"start":955.6,"duration":4.76,"text":"called Creal to extract code chains that"},{"start":958.4,"duration":3.88,"text":"lead to the dangerous things, such as"},{"start":960.36,"duration":5.0,"text":"eval."},{"start":962.28,"duration":6.6,"text":"Their reaction to turn those code chains"},{"start":965.36,"duration":7.72,"text":"into natural seed prompts using one-shot"},{"start":968.88,"duration":4.2,"text":"and chain-of-thought technique."},{"start":974.36,"duration":3.48,"text":"For example,"},{"start":975.88,"duration":4.48,"text":"if the chain looks like a calculator"},{"start":977.84,"duration":5.08,"text":"leading to eval, they are might reduce"},{"start":980.36,"duration":4.48,"text":"the prompt like"},{"start":982.92,"duration":3.32,"text":"\"Please use the calculator to evaluate 1"},{"start":984.84,"duration":3.72,"text":"+ 1.\""},{"start":986.24,"duration":5.76,"text":"This allows the agents to enter the"},{"start":988.56,"duration":3.44,"text":"right execution path."},{"start":994.08,"duration":5.68,"text":"Now, let's move to the model two,"},{"start":996.92,"duration":4.88,"text":"feedback-driven seed scheduling."},{"start":999.76,"duration":4.48,"text":"The goal here is to choose which seed"},{"start":1001.8,"duration":4.76,"text":"prompt to mutate next"},{"start":1004.24,"duration":5.16,"text":"based on runtime feedback from previous"},{"start":1006.56,"duration":2.84,"text":"executions."},{"start":1011.04,"duration":6.84,"text":"Agent Fuzz combines three scores,"},{"start":1013.88,"duration":7.2,"text":"semantic distance and penalty,"},{"start":1017.88,"duration":3.2,"text":"to make this decision."},{"start":1021.52,"duration":3.8,"text":"First,"},{"start":1022.92,"duration":4.36,"text":"the semantic score measures whether a"},{"start":1025.32,"duration":3.72,"text":"prompt's meaning is consistent with a"},{"start":1027.28,"duration":3.88,"text":"vulnerable component in the same code"},{"start":1029.04,"duration":4.2,"text":"chain."},{"start":1031.16,"duration":4.84,"text":"To calculate this, we use the code chain"},{"start":1033.24,"duration":4.68,"text":"extracted in model one."},{"start":1036.0,"duration":5.2,"text":"We feed both the code chain description"},{"start":1037.92,"duration":6.12,"text":"and the problem into the app."},{"start":1041.2,"duration":5.04,"text":"And ask whether problems intend to match"},{"start":1044.04,"duration":3.64,"text":"the function or module involved in that"},{"start":1046.24,"duration":3.4,"text":"chain."},{"start":1047.68,"duration":4.72,"text":"The closer the meaning, the higher the"},{"start":1049.64,"duration":4.32,"text":"semantic score."},{"start":1052.4,"duration":3.6,"text":"In short,"},{"start":1053.96,"duration":5.44,"text":"this score tell us that this problem"},{"start":1056.0,"duration":4.6,"text":"talk about the right thing."},{"start":1059.4,"duration":3.16,"text":"Second,"},{"start":1060.6,"duration":4.56,"text":"the distance score measures how close"},{"start":1062.56,"duration":4.52,"text":"the execution trace go to the sink"},{"start":1065.16,"duration":4.16,"text":"during run time."},{"start":1067.08,"duration":4.28,"text":"Agent Fuzz class actually code chain and"},{"start":1069.32,"duration":4.84,"text":"compares it with the ground truth sink"},{"start":1071.36,"duration":6.28,"text":"chain actually statically."},{"start":1074.16,"duration":6.2,"text":"We compute the overlap between the two."},{"start":1077.64,"duration":4.68,"text":"So, a longer matched prefix means the"},{"start":1080.36,"duration":3.48,"text":"request has reached deeper along the"},{"start":1082.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"runnable path,"},{"start":1083.84,"duration":4.28,"text":"giving a higher distance score."},{"start":1086.76,"duration":3.28,"text":"Finally,"},{"start":1088.12,"duration":5.76,"text":"the penalty score helps imbalance"},{"start":1090.04,"duration":6.16,"text":"exploration and exploitation."},{"start":1093.88,"duration":4.72,"text":"If I see a chain have already been"},{"start":1096.2,"duration":4.88,"text":"scheduled too many times,"},{"start":1098.6,"duration":4.6,"text":"its penalty increase,"},{"start":1101.08,"duration":6.12,"text":"pushing Agent Fuzz exploring new areas"},{"start":1103.2,"duration":4.0,"text":"instead of repeating the same ones."},{"start":1108.52,"duration":6.64,"text":"Putting them together, we rank all"},{"start":1110.88,"duration":6.52,"text":"candidates seeds using final score."},{"start":1115.16,"duration":4.24,"text":"This multifaceted feedback helps Agent"},{"start":1117.4,"duration":3.36,"text":"Fuzz prioritize the most of our missing"},{"start":1119.4,"duration":4.68,"text":"problems,"},{"start":1120.76,"duration":7.36,"text":"those that are both semantically correct"},{"start":1124.08,"duration":8.12,"text":"and execution-wise closer to the sink,"},{"start":1128.12,"duration":4.08,"text":"while still keeping the seed diverse."},{"start":1134.52,"duration":4.76,"text":"Here is a short example running show"},{"start":1137.4,"duration":3.68,"text":"showing why our feedback-driven seed"},{"start":1139.28,"duration":4.4,"text":"gathering helps."},{"start":1141.08,"duration":6.16,"text":"Imagine two seeds,"},{"start":1143.68,"duration":5.4,"text":"S2 and S3."},{"start":1147.24,"duration":4.84,"text":"They are look equally close in the"},{"start":1149.08,"duration":3.0,"text":"control flow graph."},{"start":1152.76,"duration":5.52,"text":"One of the end contents was"},{"start":1154.96,"duration":5.8,"text":"is permission check. While the other one"},{"start":1158.28,"duration":4.56,"text":"doesn't."},{"start":1160.76,"duration":4.44,"text":"So, only one of them actually triggers"},{"start":1162.84,"duration":5.2,"text":"code paths that match the intended"},{"start":1165.2,"duration":2.84,"text":"component."},{"start":1169.04,"duration":3.48,"text":"By bringing semantic feedback into the"},{"start":1171.08,"duration":3.72,"text":"decision,"},{"start":1172.52,"duration":4.44,"text":"Agent Frost picks the seed that's more"},{"start":1174.8,"duration":3.96,"text":"likely to reach the sink."},{"start":1176.96,"duration":4.48,"text":"So, that makes the fuzzing much more"},{"start":1178.76,"duration":2.68,"text":"efficient."},{"start":1183.88,"duration":4.88,"text":"With good seeds selected,"},{"start":1186.28,"duration":6.32,"text":"sometimes they still need fixing."},{"start":1188.76,"duration":3.84,"text":"That's where mutation comes in."},{"start":1196.28,"duration":5.08,"text":"Now, let's look at the model three,"},{"start":1198.56,"duration":4.92,"text":"sink-guided seed mutation."},{"start":1201.36,"duration":4.2,"text":"After the first seed is selected, Agent"},{"start":1203.48,"duration":6.08,"text":"Frost needs to mutate it so that the"},{"start":1205.56,"duration":4.0,"text":"prompt can truly trigger the sink."},{"start":1209.84,"duration":4.96,"text":"This model has two kinds of mutators,"},{"start":1212.76,"duration":4.24,"text":"functionality mutator and argument"},{"start":1214.8,"duration":4.68,"text":"mutator."},{"start":1217.0,"duration":4.92,"text":"First, the functionality mutator focuses"},{"start":1219.48,"duration":4.84,"text":"on semantic correction."},{"start":1221.92,"duration":4.96,"text":"Sometimes, our seed prompt fails to call"},{"start":1224.32,"duration":5.52,"text":"the right component because its meaning"},{"start":1226.88,"duration":2.96,"text":"is slightly off."},{"start":1230.68,"duration":5.16,"text":"For example, the original prompt use"},{"start":1233.44,"duration":4.96,"text":"electric search find document doesn't"},{"start":1235.84,"duration":6.6,"text":"include the idea of a permission check."},{"start":1238.4,"duration":5.64,"text":"So, the agent calls the wrong function."},{"start":1242.44,"duration":3.84,"text":"The functionality mutator rewrites the"},{"start":1244.04,"duration":4.32,"text":"prompt to better match the vulnerable"},{"start":1246.28,"duration":4.04,"text":"component's semantics."},{"start":1248.36,"duration":3.96,"text":"For instance,"},{"start":1250.32,"duration":3.84,"text":"use electric search for similarity"},{"start":1252.32,"duration":3.28,"text":"search with permission check to find a"},{"start":1254.16,"duration":2.68,"text":"doc."},{"start":1255.6,"duration":4.08,"text":"This narrows"},{"start":1256.84,"duration":6.48,"text":"the semantic gap and makes the agent"},{"start":1259.68,"duration":3.64,"text":"invoke the intended function."},{"start":1263.84,"duration":3.04,"text":"Second,"},{"start":1265.0,"duration":4.28,"text":"the argument mutator focuses on"},{"start":1266.88,"duration":5.24,"text":"constraint satisfaction."},{"start":1269.28,"duration":6.08,"text":"If if the right function is called,"},{"start":1272.12,"duration":5.36,"text":"the sink may still not be reached"},{"start":1275.36,"duration":4.96,"text":"causing some internal variable doesn't"},{"start":1277.48,"duration":5.36,"text":"meet the required constraint."},{"start":1280.32,"duration":4.64,"text":"Agent Fuzz use a concordic execution"},{"start":1282.84,"duration":5.32,"text":"based constraint solver to find what"},{"start":1284.96,"duration":3.2,"text":"values are needed."},{"start":1288.2,"duration":3.84,"text":"It extracts conditions from the"},{"start":1289.92,"duration":3.4,"text":"execution trace."},{"start":1292.04,"duration":3.84,"text":"For example,"},{"start":1293.32,"duration":4.2,"text":"sink squares a parameter that contains"},{"start":1295.88,"duration":3.88,"text":"source doc column."},{"start":1297.52,"duration":4.36,"text":"Then it mutates the problem accordingly,"},{"start":1299.76,"duration":4.48,"text":"producing something like"},{"start":1301.88,"duration":6.4,"text":"use elector with permission check find"},{"start":1304.24,"duration":5.08,"text":"doc with source doc column print one."},{"start":1308.28,"duration":3.0,"text":"This way,"},{"start":1309.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"the payload directly flows into the"},{"start":1311.28,"duration":2.48,"text":"sink."},{"start":1315.6,"duration":7.2,"text":"Now, I'd like to invite my partner to"},{"start":1318.2,"duration":4.6,"text":"walk you through the evaluation section."},{"start":1326.08,"duration":5.68,"text":">> Okay, so far, we have walked through the"},{"start":1328.72,"duration":5.6,"text":"entire workflow of Agent Fuzz. Next,"},{"start":1331.76,"duration":4.52,"text":"let's move to the evaluation part to see"},{"start":1334.32,"duration":4.76,"text":"how well Agent Fuzz performs in"},{"start":1336.28,"duration":2.8,"text":"practice."},{"start":1339.44,"duration":5.84,"text":"Let's see how we measured performance of"},{"start":1341.76,"duration":6.68,"text":"Agent Fuzz. We evaluate Agent Fuzz on 20"},{"start":1345.28,"duration":6.64,"text":"open source agents from GitHub. Each"},{"start":1348.44,"duration":6.08,"text":"repository has more than 1,000 stars."},{"start":1351.92,"duration":4.96,"text":"This give us a diverse and popular sites"},{"start":1354.52,"duration":4.56,"text":"of real projects."},{"start":1356.88,"duration":6.6,"text":"Our experiments are conducted with"},{"start":1359.08,"duration":6.16,"text":"GPT-4o as the LLM backend to ensure"},{"start":1363.48,"duration":5.52,"text":"strong tutorials and reasoning"},{"start":1365.24,"duration":5.88,"text":"capability during agent execution."},{"start":1369.0,"duration":5.12,"text":"We measure detection precision and"},{"start":1371.12,"duration":5.32,"text":"recall to assess accuracy and run"},{"start":1374.12,"duration":6.68,"text":"comparison experiments to show the"},{"start":1376.44,"duration":6.52,"text":"advantage of Agent Fuzz over baselines."},{"start":1380.8,"duration":5.04,"text":"Here are the key results from our"},{"start":1382.96,"duration":6.6,"text":"large-scale vulnerability detection."},{"start":1385.84,"duration":7.64,"text":"AgentFuzz discovered 34 vulnerabilities"},{"start":1389.56,"duration":7.4,"text":"in 14 real-world agents with 23 of them"},{"start":1393.48,"duration":6.44,"text":"already assigned CVE or issue IDs."},{"start":1396.96,"duration":6.08,"text":"Among these targets, seven agents have"},{"start":1399.92,"duration":5.52,"text":"more than 10,000 GitHub stars,"},{"start":1403.04,"duration":5.8,"text":"which means these vulnerabilities are"},{"start":1405.44,"duration":6.8,"text":"not in toy example, but in widely used"},{"start":1408.84,"duration":5.64,"text":"and influential open-source projects."},{"start":1412.24,"duration":5.32,"text":"More importantly, the detected"},{"start":1414.48,"duration":7.8,"text":"vulnerabilities include critical ones,"},{"start":1417.56,"duration":7.64,"text":"such as remote code execution and SSRF."},{"start":1422.28,"duration":5.64,"text":"These results demonstrate that AgentFuzz"},{"start":1425.2,"duration":5.84,"text":"can effectively uncover high-impact"},{"start":1427.92,"duration":5.84,"text":"security flaws in modern LLM-based"},{"start":1431.04,"duration":2.72,"text":"agents."},{"start":1433.92,"duration":3.44,"text":"Now, I will show the comparison"},{"start":1435.84,"duration":4.04,"text":"experiment."},{"start":1437.36,"duration":5.6,"text":"We compare AgentFuzz with a baseline"},{"start":1439.88,"duration":7.36,"text":"tool called LLM-Smith."},{"start":1442.96,"duration":7.44,"text":"LLM-Smith performs static backtracing"},{"start":1447.24,"duration":6.32,"text":"using PyCG and labels every backward"},{"start":1450.4,"duration":6.24,"text":"call chain as a vulnerability."},{"start":1453.56,"duration":6.16,"text":"By contrast, AgentFuzz uses static"},{"start":1456.64,"duration":5.88,"text":"tracing plus dynamic validation and"},{"start":1459.72,"duration":5.68,"text":"feedback-driven fuzzing to confirm risky"},{"start":1462.52,"duration":5.48,"text":"chains before reporting them."},{"start":1465.4,"duration":5.92,"text":"As a result, AgentFuzz improves"},{"start":1468.0,"duration":5.92,"text":"precision by 33 times and improves"},{"start":1471.32,"duration":4.2,"text":"recall by three times compared to the"},{"start":1473.92,"duration":4.04,"text":"baseline."},{"start":1475.52,"duration":5.48,"text":"This demonstrates that AgentFuzz"},{"start":1477.96,"duration":4.56,"text":"substantially reduces false positive"},{"start":1481.0,"duration":4.12,"text":"while finding many more real"},{"start":1482.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"vulnerabilities."},{"start":1485.12,"duration":5.2,"text":"Finally, we showcase a real"},{"start":1487.24,"duration":4.84,"text":"vulnerability that AgentFuzz discovered"},{"start":1490.32,"duration":5.0,"text":"in Auto-GPT,"},{"start":1492.08,"duration":5.28,"text":"a project with over 180,000"},{"start":1495.32,"duration":4.84,"text":"stars on GitHub."},{"start":1497.36,"duration":5.88,"text":"As shown in the diagram, the blue part"},{"start":1500.16,"duration":6.24,"text":"shows how the attacker gets in through a"},{"start":1503.24,"duration":6.04,"text":"prompt injection that correctly changed"},{"start":1506.4,"duration":5.08,"text":"the model's behavior and makes it follow"},{"start":1509.28,"duration":4.68,"text":"malicious instruction."},{"start":1511.48,"duration":5.72,"text":"The red part marks the moment the"},{"start":1513.96,"duration":6.04,"text":"execution reaches a dangerous function"},{"start":1517.2,"duration":5.8,"text":"where the injected content is processed"},{"start":1520.0,"duration":5.84,"text":"without any security checks."},{"start":1523.0,"duration":6.32,"text":"In this case, the model invokes the"},{"start":1525.84,"duration":6.8,"text":"Jinja2 template rendering component,"},{"start":1529.32,"duration":5.72,"text":"which becomes a vulnerable sink."},{"start":1532.64,"duration":3.6,"text":"The green part represents the malicious"},{"start":1535.04,"duration":3.88,"text":"payload,"},{"start":1536.24,"duration":6.08,"text":"which is then executed and gives the"},{"start":1538.92,"duration":6.4,"text":"attacker full control of the system."},{"start":1542.32,"duration":5.84,"text":"This case clearly demonstrates how Agent"},{"start":1545.32,"duration":4.68,"text":"Fuzz automatically generated a working"},{"start":1548.16,"duration":3.92,"text":"proof of concept,"},{"start":1550.0,"duration":4.56,"text":"detecting and confirming a real"},{"start":1552.08,"duration":7.84,"text":"high-impact remote code execution"},{"start":1554.56,"duration":8.04,"text":"vulnerability in a widely-used agent."},{"start":1559.92,"duration":4.8,"text":"We provide the source code and the white"},{"start":1562.6,"duration":4.56,"text":"paper links on this slide for your"},{"start":1564.72,"duration":4.8,"text":"reference. Please feel free to check"},{"start":1567.16,"duration":5.28,"text":"this repository and the paper for"},{"start":1569.52,"duration":4.48,"text":"implementation details and evaluation"},{"start":1572.44,"duration":3.68,"text":"artifacts."},{"start":1574.0,"duration":4.8,"text":"If you have any question or need help"},{"start":1576.12,"duration":6.0,"text":"reproducing the results, please send me"},{"start":1578.8,"duration":4.96,"text":"an email and I will be happy to assist."},{"start":1582.12,"duration":4.0,"text":"Thanks, everyone. If you have any"},{"start":1583.76,"duration":5.8,"text":"questions, feel free to come chat with"},{"start":1586.12,"duration":3.44,"text":"us later. Thank you."},{"start":1590.36,"duration":2.02,"text":">> [applause]"}]}